  "title": { "en": "Plans and dreams", "uz": "Rejalar va orzular", "ru": "Планы и мечты", "tr": "Planlar ve hayaller" },
  "goal": {
    "en": "Talk about your plans and dreams, and say why.",
    "uz": "Rejalaringiz va orzularingiz haqida gapiring, sababini ayting.",
    "ru": "Расскажите о своих планах и мечтах и объясните почему.",
    "tr": "Planlarından ve hayallerinden bahset, nedenini söyle."
  },
  "guide": "everest",
  "color": "#0F766E",
  "tip": {
    "title": { "en": "will, going to, want to", "uz": "will, going to, want to", "ru": "will, going to, want to", "tr": "will, going to, want to" },
    "body": {
      "en": "For the future put \"will\" before the verb. \"Will\" never changes: I will call, she will call. For \"no\" say will not (won't); for a question put \"will\" first: Will you come? For a plan you already have, use am / is / are + going to + verb: I am going to learn English. After want and hope use \"to\" + verb: I want to see the world. \"Because\" gives the reason: I study because I want a good job.",
      "uz": "Kelasi zamon uchun fe'ldan oldin \"will\" qo'yiladi. O'zbek tilidagi -aman, -asan, -adi qo'shimchalari o'rniga bitta alohida so'z ishlatiladi va u hech qachon o'zgarmaydi: I will call, she will call. Inkor shakli will not (won't). Savolda \"will\" oldinga chiqadi: Will you come? Oldindan o'ylangan reja (-moqchi) uchun am / is / are + going to + fe'l: I am going to learn English. want va hope dan keyin \"to\" + fe'l keladi: I want to see the world. \"Because\" (chunki) sababni bildiradi: I study because I want a good job.",
      "ru": "Будущее время образуется словом \"will\" перед глаголом. В отличие от русского, глагол не меняется по лицам: I will call, she will call. Отрицание — will not (won't). В вопросе \"will\" ставится первым: Will you come? Если это уже план или намерение («собираюсь»), говорят am / is / are + going to + глагол: I am going to learn English. После want и hope перед глаголом нужна частица \"to\": I want to see the world. \"Because\" значит «потому что»: I study because I want a good job.",
      "tr": "Gelecek zaman için fiilden önce \"will\" gelir. Türkçedeki -ecek eki yerine ayrı bir kelime kullanılır ve bu kelime hiç değişmez: I will call, she will call. Olumsuzu will not (won't). Soruda \"will\" başa gelir: Will you come? Önceden yapılmış bir plan için am / is / are + going to + fiil kullanılır: I am going to learn English. want ve hope'tan sonra \"to\" + fiil gelir (-mek istemek): I want to see the world. \"Because\" (çünkü) sebebi söyler: I study because I want a good job."
    },
    "examples": [
      { "en": "I will call you tomorrow.", "native": { "uz": "Men senga ertaga qo'ng'iroq qilaman.", "ru": "Я позвоню тебе завтра.", "tr": "Seni yarın arayacağım." } },
      { "en": "I am going to learn English.", "native": { "uz": "Men ingliz tilini o'rganmoqchiman.", "ru": "Я собираюсь учить английский.", "tr": "İngilizce öğreneceğim." } },
      { "en": "I study because I want a good job.", "native": { "uz": "Men o'qiyman, chunki yaxshi ish xohlayman.", "ru": "Я учусь, потому что хочу хорошую работу.", "tr": "Ders çalışıyorum çünkü iyi bir iş istiyorum." } }
    ]
  },
